From f3b15fab0f157ad32c402547c9d0d5719029def3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bobby Grayson <bobbbygrayson+github@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:50:52 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Make Fractal-64 Q2_0 build and compute correctly on arm64 and
 Metal

The modchip patch changes block_q2_0 to 30 bytes (d, scales[4], qs[16],
qh[8]) but leaves the upstream ARM NEON and Metal Q2_0 kernels decoding
the old 18-byte 2-bit layout. Those still compile, because d and qs keep
their names and qs is still 16 bytes, so on a Mac every Q2_0 matmul
(2.14 GiB of DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-Fractal) silently returns wrong values.

test-backend-ops -b MTL0 -o MUL_MAT -p q2_0, Metal vs CPU:
  upstream Metal kernels:  0/45 tests passed
  this commit:            45/45   (MUL_MAT_ID 75/75, GET_ROWS 4/4, CPY 2/2)

Metal: dequantize_q2_0, dequantize_q2_0_t4 and block_q_n_dot_y(q2_0) are
rewritten for the new layout. mul_mm, mul_mm_id, mul_mv_id, mul_mv_ext,
get_rows and cpy all instantiate from these three. F32 -> Q2_0 CPY is
dropped from supports_op, because quantize_q2_0 still writes the old format.
This is a correctness port: it does two device byte loads per weight.

arm64 CPU: ggml_vec_dot_q2_0_q8_0 is a new NEON/dotprod kernel for the
Fractal-64 layout (test-quantize-fns q2_0 dot error 0.014803, same as the
scalar reference). Compared with routing to the scalar generic kernel, it
doubled DeepSeek decode from 4.2 to 8.4 tok/s with layers 0-7 on CPU.

ggml_get_vec_dot_multi() now returns NULL off x86, so callers use the
per-column vec_dot. The 1xN tile kernels exist only in arch/x86/quants.c,
and without this libggml-cpu fails to link on arm64.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
